<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marta (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marta is a river of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazio">Lazio</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, flowing about 50 km from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-bolsena">Lake Bolsena</a>, its only outlet, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrrhenian-sea">Tyrrhenian Sea</a> south of Tarquinia. Its valley was a route between the Etruscan cities of the interior and the coast, and the city of Tarquinii stood on a plateau above it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marta-river.jpg" alt="Marta (river)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LigaDue · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MartaRiverBeginningMartaLazio1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
